// Your pet from a photo (v2, docs/application/features/v2-pet-from-photo-requirements.md): one
// row per photo read, kept only to count reads against the limits (R19–R22). Never the photo,
// never what the model said about it.
//
// - `device_hash`: the phone's install id (made once, kept in its Keychain), as a keyed hash
//   (HMAC with PHOTO_HASH_SECRET, R23). Set on reads made while creating a pet: 2 per phone,
//   ever. Null on a redo, which counts by account.
// - `ip_hash`: the caller's IP address, the same way. At most 6 counted reads per network a day.
// - `user_id`: set on a redo (Plus, 1 a local day), and on a creation read when signed in.
// - `local_day`: the day a redo counts against, in the phone's time zone; the UTC day otherwise.
// - `outcome`: `pending` while the model is asked (it counts, so two reads at once can't both
//   pass), then `read`, `no_pet`, `several` or `unclear`. A read that failed on our side is
//   deleted, so it never counts (R17, R20). Text, not an enum: the list is @app/contract's.
//
// Written only by the server's photo routes. The account's rows lose their user id when it is
// deleted (the hashes stay: they can't be traced back, and the phone's limit must survive).
// Not expressible here, and kept by the migrations: RLS on with no policies and nothing granted
// to the API roles.
model PetPhotoRead {
  id         String   @id @default(dbgenerated("gen_random_uuid()")) @db.Uuid
  deviceHash String?  @map("device_hash")
  ipHash     String   @map("ip_hash")
  userId     String?  @map("user_id") @db.Uuid
  context    String
  localDay   DateTime @map("local_day") @db.Date
  outcome    String
  createdAt  DateTime @default(now()) @map("created_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)
  profile    Profile? @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull, onUpdate: NoAction)

  @@index([deviceHash])
  @@index([ipHash, createdAt])
  @@index([userId, localDay])
  @@index([createdAt])
  @@map("pet_photo_reads")
}
